  "query_preview": "..\nNext 7 days (Through Sunday)...\n\nA cold front is dropping through the area from the northwest,\nbringing a wind shift and a gradual increase in relative \nhumidity. Warm temperatures will continue overnight, with breezy \nsoutherly winds ahead of the cold front, especially over the \nsoutheast where a low level jet is in place. Expect the front to \nmove through the far southeast this morning after sunrise. \nTemperatures will be about 5 to 15 degrees cooler today, relative \nto yesterday, but highs will still be in the upper 90s to around \n100 degrees, warmest over the east.\n\nWhile temperatures trend a little cooler heading into mid week as\nthe ridge axis shifts east, the eastern areas will continue to see\nhot temperatures. Very warm overnight lows and high temperatures \ninto the 100 to 105 degree range continue in far eastern Montana \nand Sheridan County, Wy into Wednesday. The Extreme Heat Warning \ncontinues today for all areas, continuing for portions of the east\non Tuesday and Wednesday due to the prolonged hot daytime \ntemperatures and warm overnight lows.\n\nOtherwise, highs in the lower to mid 90s will be common through \nthe remainder of the week into the upcoming weekend. Models \ncontinue to indicate monsoonal moisture will slide into our region\nfrom the southwest with hints of occasional weak impulses in the \nmean flow. At a minimum, this looks to bring an increase in \nrelative humidity, with a moderate chance of daily \nshowers/thunderstorms for the area, greatest over western areas. \nEnsembles continue to prog high PWATs, reaching up to 1.50 inches \nin the area from Tuesday onward. So any decent impulse in the \nmonsoonal flow may result in storms with locally heavy rainfall. \n\nFire weather...Elevated to critical fire weather conditions will\nlinger in our east into the early morning hours (especially along\nridges) due to a low level jet and slow RH recovery as the weak \nfront slides over the area. Take care not to cause a spark.\n\nSTP",
